{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas","id":1467679,"title":"V5 Kindred of the East: Clan as Dharmas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-13T07:47:24-08:00","id":1467679,"title":"V5 Kindred of the East: Clan as Dharmas","content":"So, we know KotE have been officially axed from V5, and retconned into local Vampires. <br /> <br /> I was thinking how to retcon them in the wider continuity and, as Dharmas were the defining characteristic of KotE, I was thinking of adapting them into Clans. <br /> <br /> I started reasoning, and tried to follow the trend of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom: not direct portings, but reinterpretations of the traditional concepts. <br /> <br /> These are my ideas:<br /> <br /> THE BIG 5<br /> <br /> DEVIL TIGERS: Brujah; they are splintered in a lot of different groups and are the gadflys of KotE society, and are determined to tear down the world and start anew. Their dealings with evil spirits, sacrifices and violence could be a nice tie to Carthage and the Baali. <br /> I was also thinking Tzimisce (the sadomasochistic and devilish angle is appropriate) or Lasombra (their ethic is very much the Path of Night), but Tzimisce would be too close to the original concept, whereas the Lasombra of the East were describes as a very different lot (see later). <br /> <br /> Their sorcery and judgemental attitude would also make for fine Assamites, but they're too ingrained in nearby Middle East and India, rival cultures to the Middle Kingdom. <br /> <br /> RESPLENDENT CRANES: Tzimisce. Despotic and autoritharian leaders correcting the sins of their subjects? If we discard Ventrue, which are the dominant force in the Camarilla and strong in India too, I think Tzimisce are the perfect fit. <br /> <br /> <br /> TRASHING DRAGONS: Gangrel is my choice. Hedonism and livin' la vida loca are great twists on the traditional Gangrel concept, which is, expressed instead in their emphasis on animism and shapeshifting, setting them apart from the easy choice of Toreadors. <br /> <br /> BONE FLOWERS: Lasombra. Confucian scholars doing Ancient worshipping is exactly the concept of Eastern Lasombra presented in Clanbook Lasombra Revised. <br /> Other possible choices would be Hecata and Tzimisce. <br /> <br /> THOUSAND WISPERS: Malkiavians. Their simbolism is rooted in riddles, enigmas, meditation and difficult balance, and the idea of serial impersonators seems a nice touch on Malkavians. Nosferatu and Hecata could be appropriate too. <br /> <br /> HERETICAL DHARMAS<br /> <br /> SPIRIT OF THE LIVING EARTH: Hecata. Animistic Shinto spirit traffickers with no qualms about dealing with the Infernal and uninterested into the realm of Flesh seems an appropriate adaptation of the Hecata concept, even though Abyss and the Shadowlands are a different concept. Might need customized Ceremonies or perhaps a Devotion with Animalism. <br /> <br /> FLAME OF THE RISING PHOENIX: Toreador. i have always been fond of the &quot;Toreador familyman trying hard to keep his family going&quot; of the Revised Clanbook, and they seem a very good match with the integralistic Humanism of the Phoenix. <br /> <br /> FACE OF THE GODS: Ventrue. It's an interesting twist, I think, that the Clan most associated with the Masquerade and strict hierarchies could become a group of self-centered would-be Gods. After all, far from the eyes of God-impersonating Methuselhas like Mithras and Tiamat, you can easily play the game and don't fear their wrath. <br /> <br /> SEEKERS OF THE INWARD WAY: Salubri. Tao saints striving to achieve focus and balance, and pre-dating Confucianism, are a good match for the original Golconda blueprint. <br /> <br /> SCORPION EATER: Nosferatu. Despised by all and survivalist to the extreme, they make a good equivalent for the Nosferatu hidden in their refugees and waiting for the worst to pass. <br /> <br /> THE WAY OF TEN THOUSAND SCREAMS: Ravnos. Long time enemies of the Middle Kingdom and descendants of Ravana, bent on destroying reality. <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-13-2021, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T08:16:32-08:00","id":1467682,"title":"","content":"I think it's an interesting way to handle it, though I'd consider them as Paths or Blood Cults instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T08:47:25-08:00","id":1467684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467682#post1467682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's an interesting way to handle it, though I'd consider them as Paths or Blood Cults instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely they should have also implications at the level of Convinctions and Blood Cults, they are perfect for this.<br /> <br /> This would make them even more Other in the eyes of the Camarilla, BTW.<br /> <br /> I also think they would make a fine refuge (or provide an easy assimilation) for Sabbat refugees. Dharmas would resonate with many Path Followers left without guidance by the Gehenna War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-13-2021, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T10:05:27-08:00","id":1467690,"title":"","content":"<b>Wan Kuei Suggestions</b><br /> <br /> * Obviously rename them but keep the basic Clan structure.<br /> <br /> * The Wan Kuei as &quot;we&quot; knew them were often spreading disinformation when they encountered Western Kindred and subject to weird racist stories.<br /> <br /> * The Wan Kuei are organized on a Blood Cult level and do not have an international organization but individual courts that are still vast and influential.<br /> <br /> * The Yama Kings are either Antediluvians and Demon Kings or both but no one actually &quot;fights&quot; them except in the same way the Sabbat fights them by claiming X or Y is their pawn.<br /> <br /> * Spirit magic exists among the Wan Kuei but in the same way Koldunic sorcery does. Its a lot rarer.<br /> <br /> * The Salubri are a hated and loathed bloodline for reasons unrelated to the Tremere but reflect the horrid reputation Saulot has.<br /> <br /> * The Cappadocians are still around and were never hunted by the Giovanni in this region.<br /> <br /> * Most of them are on the Bone Flower cult.<br /> <br /> * I would make the Cappadocians the <b>Jiangshi</b> and substitute Potence for Fortitude. Why? Because they have a history of tearing people apart and jumping hella high.<br /> <br /> * The Tzimsice are the rivals to the Ventrue in the region rather than a minor Clan.<br /> <br /> * The Tremere are almost nonexistent here.<br /> <br /> * The role of vampire mages is handled largely by the Tzimisce and Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> * The Banu Haqim are largely unchanged, Abrahamic, and still Muslim Caine worshipers. They do not report to Alamut, though.<br /> <br /> * The Followers of Set in the region are nonexistent but a Clan of Faith certainly does. The mainstream Setites would not even recognize their fellows here.<br /> <br /> * Ming Xiao was a Tzimsice and we just fought her in her Horrid Form. She was a Devil Tiger and not a very good one.<br /> <br /> * The entire Great Leap Outward business was done for the same reason as a Sabbat Crusade: to send the young to die out acquiring territory and relieve pressures at home. The young<br /> eventually figured out they were cannon fodder and allied with the local Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:31:02-08:00","id":1467705,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not a fan of making the Wan Kuei Cainites and frankly I do believe the Hungry Dead could be restructured while keeping the core of what they are intact.<br /> <br /> There's also the unfortunate implications that by making them also Cainites that makes the Abrahamic Faiths at least partly correct while making all other Faiths incorrect. Which is kind of a bad look. It'd be one thing if this was VtR where they completely muddied the origins of Vampires but we're not dealing with that. We're dealing with a line that ties it's origin to the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> That said, going with this notion of making Wan Kuei Cainites, I outright hate the idea of making Dharmas into Clans because they don't really work that way. They're philosophical beliefs akin to the Paths of Enlightenment. Railroading them into Clans would be like saying that only Toreadors can take the Path of Humanity while Gangrels have to be on the Path of the Beast and Ventrue to the Path of Honorable Accord. Would you restrict every member of a Clan to a specific Path of Enlightenment? No. So why should we restrict the Dharmas to specific Clans?<br /> <br /> To echo what others have said, Dharmas should be Cults with their Convictions. In V5 terms, everything about the Dharmas would be a Cult, not a Clan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:44:36-08:00","id":1467707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467705#post1467705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'm not a fan of making the Wan Kuei Cainites and frankly I do believe the Hungry Dead could be restructured while keeping the core of what they are intact.<br /> <br /> There's also the unfortunate implications that by making them also Cainites that makes the Abrahamic Faiths at least partly correct while making all other Faiths incorrect. Which is kind of a bad look. It'd be one thing if this was VtR where they completely muddied the origins of Vampires but we're not dealing with that. We're dealing with a line that ties it's origin to the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> That said, going with this notion of making Wan Kuei Cainites, I outright hate the idea of making Dharmas into Clans because they don't really work that way. They're philosophical beliefs akin to the Paths of Enlightenment. Railroading them into Clans would be like saying that only Toreadors can take the Path of Humanity while Gangrels have to be on the Path of the Beast and Ventrue to the Path of Honorable Accord. Would you restrict every member of a Clan to a specific Path of Enlightenment? No. So why should we restrict the Dharmas to specific Clans?<br /> <br /> To echo what others have said, Dharmas should be Cults with their Convictions. In V5 terms, everything about the Dharmas would be a Cult, not a Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a story a friend of mine shared and why I removed the KOTE from my games well before it became official.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kuei Jin and the &quot;Second Class Citizen&quot; problem</b><br /> <br /> I think I started to dislike the origins of the Wan Kuei in canon when it was explained to me by a friend in Hong Kong how utterly offensive they were. Basically, because they are suggesting that Asian people aren't normal people in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Bear with me.<br /> <br /> My friend stated that he and his friends in Hong Kong wanted to play Vampire: The Masquerade. They wanted to play the game that they had picked up that had the title V:TM because they wanted to play vampires. They were fans of the Lost Boys, Interview with a vampire, Dracula, and other vampire movies from the West. And my friend HATED Kindred of the East. I don't mean in a small way, I mean that it caused him to feel a kind of burning loathing of White Wolf that he struggled with because he really loved Vampire: The Masquerade and took it as a personal insult that KOTE said, effectively, &quot;I am not welcome as a player.&quot;<br /> <br /> Contrary to the belief of being more inclusive, he said the KOTE said that Asian people were not only DISTINCTLY DIFFERENT from Westerners in terms of having an afterlife, having different spiritual powers, and so on but they were an ENTIRELY DIFFERENT RACE in terms of their supernatural monsters. I suspect that being an atheist influenced him as well because he felt he was being forced into a badly written Westernized version of Chinese mythology in the very same way that people are terrified of forcing him into a very badly written version of Christian mythology. Except Christian mythology was weird and exotic and wasn't something he took nearly as seriously.<br /> <br /> He said in simple terms, &quot;I want to play a Tremere vampire in Hong Kong. I want to play in the Camarilla. I want to play in the same world as the rest of the World of Darkness. I do not want to be regulated to being their pet exotic monster which fights kung fu demons. I want to drink blood and do politics.&quot; He said that inherently the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei makes Asian gamers second class citizens in the world because they will never be the focus of the game world or what the people who pick it up want to buy. Yet the game is framed that they are the &quot;real&quot; Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> I couldn't get his perspective but it did occur to me that the Kuei Jin are every bit as heavily tied to a specific religious system, far more so than Caine and Christianity, because it effects their night to night life. If you are not a believer in traditional Chinese mythology, the Kuei Jin absolutely state that is true and force Asian gamers to deal with that in yoru unlife.<br /> <br /> A typical Kindred will never meet Caine, God, or angels.<br /> <br /> A Kuei Jin has direct experience of Hell, reincarnation, and fights monsters for Heaven.<br /> <br /> They're more like werewolves and Gaia.<br /> <br /> A Japanese immigrant friend made a different comment that he always saw the Caine myth in V:TM equivalent to Evangelion. Which is to say, &quot;I think Americans take it a lot more seriously than I do because its just weird exotic religious flavor versus someone's real religion. I mean, you don't actually believe Caine is a vampire right? Or even exists?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-13-2021, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:52:22-08:00","id":1467708,"title":"","content":"The problem IMO is that the Caine Myth is presented as fact. V5 tones this down but still. If you stop assuming the Caine Myth as automatically true, but something that was adapted to fit the Abrahamic understanding, other faiths are no longer automatically incorrect.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: The story shared above perfectly encapsulates the problems with the Wan-Kuei as a whole and why I'm glad they are no longer a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":".  Adding some comment so I don't need to add another post 11-13-2021, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T13:01:39-08:00","id":1467709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467708#post1467708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem IMO is that the Caine Myth is presented as fact. V5 tones this down but still. If you stop assuming the Caine Myth as automatically true, but something that was adapted to fit the Abrahamic understanding, other faiths are no longer automatically incorrect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which falls into the fact that in a World of Darkness, many myths are true.<br /> <br /> But in Vampire: The Masquerade, they go with the Book of Nod version.<br /> <br /> Tough call.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T13:14:46-08:00","id":1467711,"title":"","content":"I understand and agree, as I have similar issues for example in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the solution is taking out the splat. Because the problem isn't the splat. The problem is the general attitude WoD had for Asia, and that can be present with or without the splat and vice versa.<br /> <br /> So instead of eliminating the Kuei-Jin, they should have changed just their stance that their presence there somehow stops Kindred from existing in Asia, or that they can't exist outside of Asia themselves.<br /> <br /> About how to work them as Kindred, I would state their courts have access to some form of ritual that changes your inner Beast when you joins a given Dharma. So they work like clans but aren't, and in the process it becomes impossible to find out the original clan of someone. That would also explain their relationship with other local Kindred: Kuei-Jin don't Embrace, but Asia actually have other Kindred that do and the Kuei-Jin convert them.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with eliminating the Kuei-Jin is exactly the thing those players have with the religious subtext. They can live with Cainites no-prob because it is <b><i>a fucking fantasy non-sense</i></b> for them anyways. But for us that have Christianity as the prevailing religious background, the lack of other religions in the mix may leave a bitter taste in the mouth. Not on everyone's mouth, maybe, but on a lot of mouths anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 11-13-2021, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T13:17:35-08:00","id":1467712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467707#post1467707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a story a friend of mine shared and why I removed the KOTE from my games well before it became official.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kuei Jin and the &quot;Second Class Citizen&quot; problem</b><br /> <br /> I think I started to hate the origins of the Wan Kuei in canon when it was explained to me by a friend in Hong Kong how utterly offensive they were. Basically, because they are suggesting that Asian people aren't normal people in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Bear with me.<br /> <br /> My friend stated that he and his friends in Hong Kong wanted to play Vampire: The Masquerade. They wanted to play the game that they had picked up that had the title V:TM because they wanted to play vampires. They were fans of the Lost Boys, Interview with a vampire, Dracula, and other vampire movies from the West. And my friend HATED Kindred of the East. I don't mean in a small way, I mean that it caused him to feel a kind of burning loathing of White Wolf that he struggled with because he really loved Vampire: The Masquerade and took it as a personal insult that KOTE said, effectively, &quot;I am not welcome as a player.&quot;<br /> <br /> Contrary to the belief of being more inclusive, he said the KOTE said that Asian people were not only DISTINCTLY DIFFERENT from Westerners in terms of having an afterlife, having different spiritual powers, and so on but they were an ENTIRELY DIFFERENT RACE in terms of their supernatural monsters. I suspect that being an atheist influenced him as well because he felt he was being forced into a badly written Westernized version of Chinese mythology in the very same way that people are terrified of forcing him into a very badly written version of Christian mythology. Except Christian mythology was weird and exotic and wasn't something he took nearly as seriously.<br /> <br /> He said in simple terms, &quot;I want to play a Tremere vampire in Hong Kong. I want to play in the Camarilla. I want to play in the same world as the rest of the World of Darkness. I do not want to be regulated to being their pet exotic monster which fights kung fu demons. I want to drink blood and do politics.&quot;<br /> <br /> He said that inherently the Kuei Jin/Wan Kuei makes Asian gamers second class citizens in the world because they will never be the focus of the game world or what the people who pick it up want to buy. Yet the game is framed that they are the &quot;real&quot; Kindred of the East.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't disagree with that. Like I said, I think the Hungry Dead can be redone and restructured but I don't think they should be remade as Cainites as that leaves it's own unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd say the easiest and shortest way to deal with this is break down the barriers dividing Cainite and Hungry Dead. Both groups have pushed into the others territory over the last couple centuries and have since come to intermingle with the rise of Globalization. Just as we have Hungry Dead as Anarchs or Cam, we have Cainites following Dharmic paths and living in Hungry Dead Courts. The Prince of Hong Kong doesn't care if you're Cainite or Hungry Dead, whether you follow Humanity or a Dharma just as long as you're loyal to them and the Camarilla, and obey the rules. Their Quincunx counterpart will be much the same in that regard. Of course, both will likely be biased towards their particular breed of undead but that's nothing new for Kindred.<br /> <br /> Hell, with the rise of Cults in V5, bringing the Dharmas to Cainites wouldn't be that out of place.<br /> <br /> Also of course, the removal of any regional and ethnic requirements to become a Hungry Dead. Anyone, anywhere can become a Hungry Dead. Those in Eastern Asia (and potentially elsewhere) just had the advantage of relative isolation from Cainites back in the Bronze Age to lay a foundation for their societies and endure future conflicts with Cainities. Their counterparts in Europe and the Middle East didn't have that and were basically treated as Caitiff/Thin-bloods, living as small groups on the fringes of Cainite Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T13:38:03-08:00","id":1467716,"title":"","content":"I really like all these ideas. I might just delete the Wan Kuei entirely and replace them with regular Cainites, but retool the Dharmas as Asian Paths of Enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T15:25:34-08:00","id":1467729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467711#post1467711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand and agree, as I have similar issues for example in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the solution is taking out the splat. Because the problem isn't the splat. The problem is the general attitude WoD had for Asia, and that can be present with or without the splat and vice versa.<br /> <br /> So instead of eliminating the Kuei-Jin, they should have changed just that their presence there somehow stops Kindred from existing in Asia, or that they can't exist outside of Asia themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that make it any better? East Asians still likely want to play the standard clans, that they likely have the most exposure to, in their home cities without having to trample over canon. Just now instead of them being an &quot;exotic&quot; enemy for western kindred, they are simply a canon reason for no one playing Cainites in East Asia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467711#post1467711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems with eliminating the Kuei-Jin is exactly the thing those players have with the religious subtext. They can live with Cainites no-prob because it is <b><i>a fucking fantasy non-sense</i></b> for them anyways. But for us that have Christianity as the prevailing religious background, the lack of other religions in the mix may leave a bitter taste in the mouth. Not on everyone's mouth, maybe, but on a lot of mouths anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That problem stems from Caine being OOC presented as fact. Adding extra mystical &quot;vampires&quot; that only exist in Asia with really different themes, making them all bound to be believers in their local prevalent religion doesn't really solve anything aside from making the setting less cohesive.<br /> <br /> Honestly, its not far from making western kindred all bound to their local church, the reason they exist being that they weren't given a proper burial, leading you to meeting God and being sent back in order to fight the Devil with the power of the communion and to defend the Pope or someshit like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":".  grammar. 11-13-2021, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T15:32:19-08:00","id":1467730,"title":"","content":"I handled the issue of Abrahmic Christianity in my games a bit differently than other posters. Despite the fact I'm a Abrahmic believer and most of my players are atheist, I decided that I would make a lot of versions of the story of Caine and Lilith spread across different cultural bends in my game.<br /> <br /> Here's what my Noddist PC had a debate with Beckett about.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Followers of Set think Caine is cultural appropriation</b>: A fratricide where brother kills brother and the highest god curses the murderer. Are we talking about Caine and Able or Set and Osiris. The Followers of Set have a fairly decent argument that the Caine and Able story is Jewish Kindred altering their mythology for their own culture. Interestingly, I added some ambiguity that there was once a heretical sect of Folowers of Set that argued that &quot;Set&quot; is not actually Set.<br /> <br /> Yes, there were Followers of Set who believed that Set the Antediluvian is actually <b>Wepwawet</b> or <b>Typhon</b>, a Apophis-worshiping Abomination (literally an Embraced Silent Strider) or <b>Sobek the Embraced Mokole</b> which would explain why the Followers of Set have confusion over 1st and 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Romulus and Remus</b>: The Roman Ventrue believed that they were descended from the infamous Wolf Brothers of Rome. According to their legend, though, Romulus murdered his brother but was cursed by Jupiter, Helios, and other gods in retaliation. They received succor from Pluto and Nyx the Goddess of the Night who fills the role of Lilith in their culture.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Werewolf Legends</b>: The Garou have a mythological origin for vampires that the First Ronin and the first Metis was also the First Abomination. The Garou murdered him for his disgusting nature but a Gurahl used his resurrection ritual to bring him back. However, so Wyrm tainted and disgusting was the first Metis that he emerged as a monster. This story is considered nakedly racist against Metis and not repeated much anymore but was used to justify the War of Rage. It was the Garou's way of blaming vampirism on other shifters.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Hecate</b>: The Greek Goddess takes the role of Lilith and Caine both in this legend, raising one of her lovers from the dead and proceeding to teach him the secret of avoiding it as well as the arts of the gods. He promptly shares it with his brothers and sisters, creating the Antediluvians. The gods seeing the theft of ambrosia and the Antediluvains passing themselves off as the Olympians, curse them and banish Hecate from Olympus. In this story, there is no such thing as the 2nd generation.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>The Path of Evil Revelations</b>: The Path of Evil Revelations teaches that Cainites were created by mortal worshipers of Hell making deals with the Archdemons and that all of the Antediluvians offered their children's souls to keep themselves immortal, which they would harvest regularly. There's 13 founders of the Baali in this version and Nergal, Shaitan, and others are effectively apocryphal. The other vampires are just in denial of their true nature, perhaps because the Path of Evil Revelations says that not only are they damned but they just exist to be sacrifices at the next cyclical Gehenna.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Caine is a Risen</b>: Caine is just a Western Risen that learned how to feed on Blood for Corpus and pass on his condition. He's nothing particularly special, just old as fuck.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Norse mythology</b>: Odin became the first vampire when he died on a tree in exchange for greater wisdom. This was so that he could gain the secret to surviving Ragnarok but was cursed with the need for blood but could create great warriors with furious rage to battle the Lupines (Children of Fenris), the Giants (Fae), and other supernaturals. All of the gods are vampires and you should be proud not ashamed of what you are. Gangrel add further that the Christian God is actually Surtur and trying to weaken humanity for slaughter.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>The Legend of the Rakshasa</b>: Ravana and his Rakshasa are the Kindred and have the divinely appointed task of tormenting and tempting mortals into sin as well as inflicting pain as well as misery on them. Unfortunately, the other Kindred have fallen away from their task due to passing their gift onto the unworthy. The Antediluvians are all Ravana's sons and daughters but according to Ravnos teachings, anyone can become an Antediluvian by drinking enough blood and living long enough.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos notably believe the Antediluvian killed in India was not the first vampire but that Ravana was killed by Rama in ancient times. Which is why wooden stakes and the Sun hurt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-13-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T17:30:33-08:00","id":1467739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467729#post1467729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that make it any better?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, I miss typed. My intended phrasing was <i>&quot;changed just their stance that&quot;</i>, so I actually meant the opposite.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467729#post1467729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That problem stems from Caine being OOC presented as fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still the problem may be addressed with creatures that don't follow Noddist reasoning as existing, and other religions being a possible explanation for something.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, adding other creatures that follow their own rules adds variety to the setting itself, and if we don't assume Caine as objective truth I don't see how the Kindred not being the only undead monsters in the world makes the setting less cohesive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467729#post1467729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, its not far from making western kindred all bound to their local church, the reason they exist being that they weren't given a proper burial, leading you to meeting God and being sent back in order to fight the Devil with the power of the communion and to defend the Pope or someshit like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, never said they should exist in exactly the same way.<br /> <br /> My proposal is simply that the Kuei-Jin are a valid element of the setting and should stay in the setting. Not as Kindred of the East, but simply as their own thing. And players everywhere should be able to play as either a &quot;Cainite&quot; or a Kuei-Jin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T18:21:43-08:00","id":1467747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467739#post1467739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't, I miss typed. My intended phrasing was <i>&quot;changed just their stance that&quot;</i>, so I actually meant the opposite.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, it makes sense now. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind them being their own thing, spread everywhere. Personally, I agree with the old idea of tying them to Wraith instead of Vampire, making them something like the Risen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T19:33:23-08:00","id":1467749,"title":"","content":"I just made Hungry Dead a worldwide phenomenon but they are outcompeted by Cainites because they 'breed' like cockroachs and take a tenth of the time to become relatively stable; the vast majority of Hungry Dead likely are killed as Wights if they rise in Kindred dominated regions and no one is any the wiser. <br /> <br /> Obviously I did a fair bit of work to refit Hungry Ghosts as presented in KotE Core because they are 100% Sinocentric ( and only Central Mainland at that) and pay only bare lip service to any of the hundreds of other cultures in the region, despite the semi-random use of Japanese terms. But luckily alternate Dharmas/Paths are easy enough to homebrew and ' Shintai'/Disciplines are even easier to brew based on folklore and legend.<br /> <br /> That said I find the Hungry Ghost model works way better for, non-movie/novel based European folkloric vampires and those of other regions like Oceania, South America, Africa, Pre-Colonial North America etc.<br /> <br /> All of the KotE books beyond the core acknowledge the existence of Cainite populations throughout Asia so I'm not sure why that keeps getting brought up. Its a big world there's room for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T19:41:44-08:00","id":1467750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467749#post1467749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the KotE books beyond the core acknowledge the existence of Cainite populations throughout Asia so I'm not sure why that keeps getting brought up. Its a big world there's room for both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The early books took a very specific task of, &quot;The Kindred of the East kill Cainites whenever they find them and have no association with them while dominating the region.&quot; So much so that they stated the Ravnos Antediluvian was awakened by the thousands of Ravnos they had killed over the years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T20:35:03-08:00","id":1467756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467750#post1467750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The early books took a very specific task of, &quot;The Kindred of the East kill Cainites whenever they find them and have no association with them while dominating the region.&quot; So much so that they stated the Ravnos Antediluvian was awakened by the thousands of Ravnos they had killed over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do I really need to go through and find the dozens of sentences that speak on Cainite populations throughout Asia? Throughout the KotE ( and VtM ) line Cainite populations within Asia are mentioned relatively to very often.<br /> <br /> It is an established fact that they exist within the setting.<br /> <br /> They were mainly attacked because A) The Quincunx are racist fuckwits to literally everyone. B) Some Disciplines cause damage to Dragon Lines/Nests <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, based on my own changes to the setting and not canon, I'd also add C) Cainites are cockroaches. You let a small group in and given the opportunity they'll reproduce at an exponential rate and try and wipe you out. Just like they have mostly acheived throughout Europe, Africa, North America and the Middle East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 11-13-2021, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T20:57:23-08:00","id":1467757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467756#post1467756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do I really need to go through and find the dozens of sentences that speak on Cainite populations throughout Asia? Throughout the KotE ( and VtM ) line Cainite populations within Asia are mentioned relatively to very often.<br /> <br /> It is an established fact that they exist within the setting.<br /> <br /> They were mainly attacked because A) The Quincunx are racist fuckwits to literally everyone. B) Some Disciplines cause damage to Dragon Lines/Nests<br /> <br /> Personally, based on my own changes to the setting and not canon, I'd also add C) Cainites are cockroaches. You let a small group in and given the opportunity they'll reproduce at an exponential rate and try and wipe you out. Just like they have mostly acheived throughout Europe, Africa, North America and the Middle East.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exist is not the question.<br /> <br /> At war with a massive number of KOTE and cut off from the rest of vampire society is another.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T21:06:47-08:00","id":1467759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467749#post1467749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because they are 100% Sinocentric ( and only Central Mainland at that) and pay only bare lip service to any of the hundreds of other cultures in the region</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair description of old WW view on Asia. It's basically Mainland Hun China With Tokugawa Samurai and Ninjas.<br /> <br /> And that was actually above average for the time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467749#post1467749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I find the Hungry Ghost model works way better for, non-movie/novel based European folkloric vampires and those of other regions like Oceania, South America, Africa, Pre-Colonial North America etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can straight up say it works better for folkloric undead, period, because it does.<br /> <br /> The thing we call a Vampire isn't in any sense a folkloric creature, it is strictly a pop culture phenomenon created out of a few key works of great influence, namely The Vampyre (Polidori), Dracula (Bram Stoker), Nosferatu (Murnau), The Vampire Chronicles (Anne Rice) and indeed, yours truly, Vampire: the Masquerade (Rein-Hagen). Together those works created the entire vampire mythos out of nothing.<br /> <br /> So, while it isn't a meaningless feat in any sense, the rules for the Kindred aren't actually good at representing anything but itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467749#post1467749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the KotE books beyond the core acknowledge the existence of Cainite populations throughout Asia so I'm not sure why that keeps getting brought up.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, but I personally only saw the books being adamant about the utter revulsion the Kuei-Jin have towards the Cainites and how effective they have been in their war against &quot;western&quot; vampires, to a point that the few Kindred described as living in East Asia are either marginalized and hunted, or live in a frontier war with the Kuei-Jin. They are there, but don't have a functional society.<br /> <br /> But I'm definitely not sure, so if things have changed, I'm interested in knowing more.<br /> <br /> And aside STs that like to play it at ten times the officially recommended number, I don't see how a population that takes pain to keep themselves at a ratio of 1:100k can be described as cockroaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T00:14:50-08:00","id":1467774,"title":"","content":"If they are still cainites then what's the point? They would be a false delusion against the canonical christian truth. The point of KotE was being not cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T04:26:04-08:00","id":1467783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467774#post1467774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are still cainites then what's the point? They would be a false delusion against the canonical christian truth. The point of KotE was being not cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have succinctly pointed out why people hate the Kuei Jin, Taggie.<br /> <br /> Asian gamers want to play vampires and were asked to play Daoist zombies. They want to have a culture that would allow them to be part of the gameline that they bought. Same as the Laibon and Ashirra. You're asking a different question and wanting a solution to a problem that is not necessarily the one being asked about.<br /> <br /> Your problem: Too much Christianity is right.<br /> <br /> Their problem: Not enough Asian Camarilla, Anarchs, Sabbat, and roleplaying opportunities.<br /> <br /> With a side order of: Daoist mythology is right if you're Hindu, Shinto, Islamic, or atheist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T06:25:43-08:00","id":1467786,"title":"","content":"How much Christian myth does V5 actually confirm? It isn't made for the sort of game where your coterie meets Caine himself and personally ends Gehenna, one way or another. If Chinese kindred said that the Christian myth surrounding kindred origins was just western embellishment, would <i>we </i>have proof to refute that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T08:43:08-08:00","id":1467794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467705#post1467705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'm not a fan of making the Wan Kuei Cainites and frankly I do believe the Hungry Dead could be restructured while keeping the core of what they are intact.<br /> <br /> There's also the unfortunate implications that by making them also Cainites that makes the Abrahamic Faiths at least partly correct while making all other Faiths incorrect. Which is kind of a bad look. It'd be one thing if this was VtR where they completely muddied the origins of Vampires but we're not dealing with that. We're dealing with a line that ties it's origin to the Old Testament.<br /> <br /> That said, going with this notion of making Wan Kuei Cainites, I outright hate the idea of making Dharmas into Clans because they don't really work that way. They're philosophical beliefs akin to the Paths of Enlightenment. Railroading them into Clans would be like saying that only Toreadors can take the Path of Humanity while Gangrels have to be on the Path of the Beast and Ventrue to the Path of Honorable Accord. Would you restrict every member of a Clan to a specific Path of Enlightenment? No. So why should we restrict the Dharmas to specific Clans?<br /> <br /> To echo what others have said, Dharmas should be Cults with their Convictions. In V5 terms, everything about the Dharmas would be a Cult, not a Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dharmas have structure, concept and prominence that are equivalent to the role of Clans in Western society: O dp agree that they are better as Path equivalents, however if we go with no KotE, but with a KotEK situation, there is significant conceptual overlapping and they provide an easy way of tailoring Clans to an Asian landscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T08:45:23-08:00","id":1467795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467711#post1467711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand and agree, as I have similar issues for example in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the solution is taking out the splat. Because the problem isn't the splat. The problem is the general attitude WoD had for Asia, and that can be present with or without the splat and vice versa.<br /> <br /> So instead of eliminating the Kuei-Jin, they should have changed just their stance that their presence there somehow stops Kindred from existing in Asia, or that they can't exist outside of Asia themselves.<br /> <br /> About how to work them as Kindred, I would state their courts have access to some form of ritual that changes your inner Beast when you joins a given Dharma. So they work like clans but aren't, and in the process it becomes impossible to find out the original clan of someone. That would also explain their relationship with other local Kindred: Kuei-Jin don't Embrace, but Asia actually have other Kindred that do and the Kuei-Jin convert them.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with eliminating the Kuei-Jin is exactly the thing those players have with the religious subtext. They can live with Cainites no-prob because it is <b><i>a fucking fantasy non-sense</i></b> for them anyways. But for us that have Christianity as the prevailing religious background, the lack of other religions in the mix may leave a bitter taste in the mouth. Not on everyone's mouth, maybe, but on a lot of mouths anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really an elegant solution and also an awesome plot device: basically the &quot;Kindred of the East&quot; would be a society of Caitiffs based on cooperation between different Blood Cults, something really unique and also quite terrifying for the Western Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T09:43:56-08:00","id":1467798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467786#post1467786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Christian myth does V5 actually confirm? It isn't made for the sort of game where your coterie meets Caine himself and personally ends Gehenna, one way or another. If Chinese kindred said that the Christian myth surrounding kindred origins was just western embellishment, would <i>we </i>have proof to refute that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the big issue is the Kuei Jin are like the Garou in that they are 100% right and the lowliest member knows it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T11:58:17-08:00","id":1467807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467783#post1467783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asian gamers want to play vampires and were asked to play Daoist zombies. They want to have a culture that would allow them to be part of the gameline that they bought. Same as the Laibon and Ashirra. <b>You're asking a different question and wanting a solution to a problem that is not necessarily the one being asked about.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not it.<br /> <br /> Instead, is that the solution proposed creates another problem.<br /> <br /> Asian players face a lot of problems because WW was &quot;orientalist&quot; to the extreme. That's true, for sure.<br /> <br /> Yet removing the splat changes nothing because none of the problems is inherent to the splat itself. What it does change is to remove one of the few in-universe evidences against Noddism, which isn't a problem for them, but is a problem for us.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, for them Christianity is exotic and fantasy-like anyways. Not a cultural presence with a history of bad interactions wit other faiths that still results in frequent religious-based violence of all kinds and stomps other beliefs frequently while selling to itself a narrative of martyrdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T12:33:31-08:00","id":1467811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467749#post1467749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I did a fair bit of work to refit Hungry Ghosts as presented in KotE Core because they are 100% Sinocentric ( and only Central Mainland at that) and pay only bare lip service to any of the hundreds of other cultures in the region, despite the semi-random use of Japanese terms. But luckily alternate Dharmas/Paths are easy enough to homebrew and ' Shintai'/Disciplines are even easier to brew based on folklore and legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think one could easily take Dharma and give it regional variations. They tend to be fairly broad philosophical concepts drawn more from a particular alignment. And as we see in the Dharma Books they are different schools of thought within them. <br /> <br /> The Resplendent Cranes might be a tricky due to it's more rigid nature and the heavy inspiration it draws from Legalism and Confucianism. Out of universe of course. In universe the Dharma is said to predate before philosophies. But I don't think it would be impossible to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467786#post1467786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Christian myth does V5 actually confirm? It isn't made for the sort of game where your coterie meets Caine himself and personally ends Gehenna, one way or another. If Chinese kindred said that the Christian myth surrounding kindred origins was just western embellishment, would <i>we </i>have proof to refute that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for starters, once again presents the story of Caine and several occasions refers to Kindred as the 'descendants/children of Caine' just as previous editions do. In fact they have a whole section in V5 talking about the legend. While they do throw out that most in the Camarilla think he's nothing more than a myth, they never present any alternatives.<br /> <br /> Because that's the thing, the story of Caine both in and out of universe has become so utterly linked to VtM that there really is no alternative. And if they attempted to bring out some new alternative most are going to view it as fake because Caine has been so build up as the origin of VtM Vampires in the setting.<br /> <br /> Honestly I think that's a big reason why VtR did away with Generation and a common origin story for their vampires, so they could have vampires across the world with wildly different beliefs in their origins without anyone being right or wrong about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467794#post1467794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dharmas have structure, concept and prominence that are equivalent to the role of Clans in Western society: O dp agree that they are better as Path equivalents, however if we go with no KotE, but with a KotEK situation, there is significant conceptual overlapping and they provide an easy way of tailoring Clans to an Asian landscape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the vampires of KotEK are specifically a branch of Cainite vampires and not they're own thing like the Wan Kuei are. The vampires of KotEK were written with Clans, the Wan Kuei were not. There are only two breeds of Hungry Dead and the Yulan-jin. The latter being a mutant strain of Hungry Dead who's souls are not properly anchored to their bodies and end up jumping from corpse to corpse.<br /> <br /> If you want to replace the Wan Kuei with Cainites than simply put the Clans there and give them the Dharmas as a Paths of Enlightenment. Like I said before, attempting to link Dharmas to Clans is like linking Paths of Enlightenment to Clans. Like you suggested that Gangrel should be Thrashing Dragons. But at the same time plenty of Toreadors would also fit the Dragon mindset to say nothing of random members of other Clans with a similar mindset. Frankly the Thousand Whispers Dharma does not work as anything but a philosophical belief.<br /> <br /> Again, it's like saying that only Toreadors can have the Path of Humanity and the Path of Humanity can only be followed by Toreadors. Would that work? No. By that same token it would not work for the Dharmas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T12:51:21-08:00","id":1467812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467807#post1467807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's not it.<br /> <br /> Instead, is that the solution proposed creates another problem.<br /> <br /> Asian players face a lot of problems because WW was &quot;orientalist&quot; to the extreme. That's true, for sure.<br /> <br /> Yet removing the splat changes nothing because none of the problems is inherent to the splat itself. What it does change is to remove one of the few in-universe evidences against Noddism, which isn't a problem for them, but is a problem for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the deep distaste some posters have for Abrahamic faiths as game material but aside from saying, &quot;No, the Caine myth is not true&quot; I feel like there's absolutely nothing that can be done with it. The game developers used Christian mythology as a basis for their vampire curse and it is front and center so that you can't attack it sideways with the Kuei Jin. You would have to directly offer alternate origins and state that none of them are objectively incorrect. Nothing else will do anything here and we shouldn't pretend otherwise.<br /> <br /> There's also a problem with this argument because the Kuei Jin have absolutely nothing to do with Noddism and do absolutely nothing as an argument against it. They are completely unrelated to the Curse of Caine and do nothing to refute it because they are a different species. It's like arguing Changelings or Garou are evidence against the Church of Caine. If they had an origin, basically if they were VAMPIRES, they would be able to argue it.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos and Followers of Set aren't given much respect but they are clearly Kindred and thus can argue that Caine is a silly myth. But the Kuei Jin are not Kindred so they have absolutely nothing to say on the subject.<br /> <br /> They are a different splat and that restricts any benefit they could have to what you're suggesting. To start with what you need, you'd need to make the Kuei Jin into members of the existing 13 Clans and THEN present a non-Christian origin for them. As such, I don't think Taggie's belief works because they're too removed from Cainite existence to actually be a Cainite rebuttal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, you know, for them Christianity is exotic and fantasy-like anyways. Not a cultural presence with a history of bad interactions wit other faiths that still results in frequent religious-based violence of all kinds and stomps other beliefs frequently while selling to itself a narrative of martyrdom. </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to note that V:TM was created as a backlash against Georgia based Bible Belt fundamentalism in the counter-culture district of Atlanta. In a very real way, it was created as art driven by anger against the religious rights repression. The intimacy of the satire and anger is inherent to using it in-game, though. Removing it may make for a less offensive narrative but might make it lesser as a work of art. You're free to disagree, though.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of how the writers of Hellblazer were continually hounded by DC Comics to stop including angels in their comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-14-2021, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:33:28-08:00","id":1467818,"title":"","content":"@CT Phipps, what once may have been meant as satire now looks like apologetics and identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:53:01-08:00","id":1467821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467807#post1467807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet removing the splat changes nothing because none of the problems is inherent to the splat itself. What it does change is to remove one of the few in-universe evidences against Noddism, which isn't a problem for them, but is a problem for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not much evidence against noddism. It is a completely different existence, only linked together because they are bothe &quot;vampires&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467807#post1467807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, you know, for them Christianity is exotic and fantasy-like anyways. Not a cultural presence with a history of bad interactions wit other faiths that still results in frequent religious-based violence of all kinds and stomps other beliefs frequently while selling to itself a narrative of martyrdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the problem is that Caine was for a long time sold as the one true origin. And anyway, I feel people look far too deep into the Caine thing. Cain is a minor character that never shows up again in the Holy books, he doesn't get super vampire powers or an encounter with Lilith or anything of the sort. As far as we know, God is just a jerk in WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:55:34-08:00","id":1467822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467818#post1467818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@CT Phipps, what once may have been meant as satire now looks like apologetics and identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone sees a different ocean.<br /> <br /> But I should point out the biggest point of the early edition of the game is you are damned through something arbitrary and that has made you a monster. The God of Vampire: The Masquerade can be apologized for but the premise of the game is that he's done something utterly awful to humanity. And you specifically. It's an interesting case that the Gnostics are probably the LEAST incoherent religious interpretation of God because no decent deity would inflict such evil on their creations.<br /> <br /> This was a central theme in the Noddist Christianity of 1st Edition, which bluntly all but establishes God is evil or at least operating from a wholly alien morality. V5 underscored it because it makes it clear even the nicest vampires are forced into a predestined evil and horror by their biology.<br /> <br /> This is what Mark Rein Hagen was going for, an existentialist worldview created from &quot;Yes, the supernatural and God in particular exist but they do not care about you and indeed, have cursed you.&quot;<br /> <br /> That may be deeper than other gamers wish to go, however, as its a pretty big bar to set that, &quot;Yes, no matter what, you exist in a world where the Abrahmic deity exists. Sole god or part of a multitude.&quot; Even if he's an asshole, it's an endorsement of a kind.<br /> <br /> <b>Random Aside</b><br /> <br /> A recent video on Slasher movies was made by Renegade Cut and said they maintained a Reagan-esque morality of sexual and religious oppression. Renegade Cut got TORN TO RIBBONS because they didn't seem to realize that associating Jason, Freddy, and Michael Myers with the religious right wasn't an ENDORSEMENT of the latter but a condemnation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iBA3Hiqms5M\" data-code=\"iBA3Hiqms5M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iBA3Hiqms5M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But it's still a common view of slasher films that because sex=death and horny smoking teens get murdered that it was supporting their view. I see a similar view with the World of Darkness where Religious Institutions, God, and Damnation are inherently questioned. They are real in the setting but the game puts you in the place of those furiously railing against the inherent unfairness and injustice of it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-14-2021, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T14:17:01-08:00","id":1467824,"title":"","content":"I have two sort of Abrahamic gods in my WoD. One is a truly ancient pangender being of pure light known as the One or the Absolute. Along with Gaia the mother goddess, the One created the earth and possibly the whole universe.<br /> <br /> The second god, a much younger definitely male god, is known as El, the Demiurge or simply God. He created the Garden of Eden, cursed Cain(e) and went to war against the Fallen.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m Wiccan, but I was raised in an Abrahamic faith and wanted to create a cosmos that included the best and worst parts of both religions. I don\u2019t know enough about Asian faiths to include them, but I think Buddhism believes in a creator similar to my conception of the One. This is just my own head canon, but I\u2019ve never had a player tell me they felt offended by my cosmology.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I deleted the Wan Kuei from my WoD once I reviewed some of the discussions on this forum and learned that they did not exist in V5, and also agreed with the excellent reasons given by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> and others why they should not be included. I did keep the original Wan Xian because they\u2019re explicitly mentioned in the Apocalyptic Record Kickstarter, but I made it so that the August Personage of Jade destroyed them as punishment for their rebellion rather than transforming them into vampires.<br /> <br /> Thanks for listening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T14:28:54-08:00","id":1467827,"title":"","content":"Cool beans, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26996_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26996\" data-vbnamecard=\"26996\">Amethyst</a> <br /> <br /> In my own games, I have a few other takes on God but the one that I generally do for DEMON: THE FALLEN and V:TM that touch on religion is God is GONE. Heaven is empty and the angels are all missing. The mages speculate that God broke himself/herself up into pieces and those pieces were given to humanity as Avatars. In other words, Humanity has the power of CreationTM. Other more cynical types believe the Creator has simply left for an alternate universe or destroyed itself.<br /> <br /> My Devil character had the insane plan that he wanted to replace God....so he could help as many people as possible.<br /> <br /> Which is an interesting subversion of such a deity-esque belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T16:28:06-08:00","id":1467832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467822#post1467822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I should point out the biggest point of the early edition of the game is you are damned through something arbitrary and that has made you a monster. The God of Vampire: The Masquerade can be apologized for but the premise of the game is that he's done something utterly awful to humanity. And you specifically. It's an interesting case that the Gnostics are probably the LEAST incoherent religious interpretation of God because no decent deity would inflict such evil on their creations.<br /> <br /> This was a central theme in the Noddist Christianity of 1st Edition, which bluntly all but establishes God is evil or at least operating from a wholly alien morality. V5 underscored it because it makes it clear even the nicest vampires are forced into a predestined evil and horror by their biology.<br /> <br /> This is what Mark Rein Hagen was going for, an existentialist worldview created from &quot;Yes, the supernatural and God in particular exist but they do not care about you and indeed, have cursed you.&quot;<br /> <br /> That may be deeper than other gamers wish to go, however, as its a pretty big bar to set that, &quot;Yes, no matter what, you exist in a world where the Abrahmic deity exists. Sole god or part of a multitude.&quot; Even if he's an asshole, it's an endorsement of a kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this, but I don't think it's really that central to VtM. The Camarilla doesn't talk much about God. I don't think even the Sabbat does, for all they have to say about Caine. He's a key figure in several Paths, but in different ways and not at all in some. Whereas VtR proposed the same idea, but without confirming it.<br /> <br /> So I don't want to invalidate a WoD with a cruel Abrahamic God, but the myth can coexist with other possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T17:59:54-08:00","id":1467843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467832#post1467832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love this, but I don't think it's really that central to VtM. The Camarilla doesn't talk much about God. I don't think even the Sabbat does, for all they have to say about Caine. He's a key figure in several Paths, but in different ways and not at all in some. Whereas VtR proposed the same idea, but without confirming it.<br /> <br /> So I don't want to invalidate a WoD with a cruel Abrahamic God, but the myth can coexist with other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'm being mono-focused on the Caine myth and the Book of Nod legend they had. Playing vampires was in 1992 a pretty radical concept as was incorporating real life mythology. Why? Well, this was just after D&amp;D flipped its lid trying to cater to the BADD crowd as well as stripping &quot;demons&quot; and &quot;devils&quot; from the game as well as insisting it was family friendly as well as good for children.<br /> <br /> V:TM found itself in a very good place because it appealed to those college aged gamers (and younger seeking to ape college aged gamers) who wanted to rebel as well as were perfectly willing to wrap themselves in what was considered occult by a not-insignificant section of the population. The use of the Caine myth and playing the &quot;bad guys&quot; and THE DAMNED was a braver choice than perhaps those who consider it all harmless fun might have believed.<br /> <br /> Its kind of fascinating that V:TM never generated that kind of controversy as Dungeons and Dragons did--perhaps because it wore its defiance of social norms openly.<br /> <br /> (I mean it did generate quite a bit but not nearly as much)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T21:43:47-08:00","id":1467855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467812#post1467812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like arguing Changelings or Garou are evidence against the Church of Caine. If they had an origin, basically if they were VAMPIRES, they would be able to argue it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two key points here that make a lot of difference. Although I agree that they are a minor benefit, far from a solution to the core problem. But that out of the way, here's the thing:<br /> <br /> First, they have a difference from other splats in relation to Vampires. <b>They are meant to be canon in Vampire as is</b>. Remember that each line is its own thing to a degree. The cosmology of an entire game line doesn't necessarily translate to others directly. But <b>KotE isn't a separate line, it's a Masquerade supplement</b>. So whatever is said in their book, is just as canon in VtM.<br /> <br /> Second, <b>the problem isn't Caine</b>. The problem is Christianity appearing to be more valid or more real than other religions. In this regard, Caine and the Book of Nod are only a problem as evidence that the Old Testament is real. So any counter evidence <b>for the bible</b> that weaken this relation helps.<br /> <br /> As the Japanese player put it very well, the Book of Nod itself is actually just a fictional mythology and means nothing to anyone in real life. But the bible does.<br /> <br /> But again, this is actually just a minor benefit. You're absolutely right that the Ravnos, Followers of Set, and any other group that presents alternate myths for the &quot;Cainites&quot; are a better fit, and I think their myths should get more weight behind them to actually be able to replace Noddism as plot devices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467812#post1467812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to note that V:TM was created as a backlash against Georgia based Bible Belt fundamentalism in the counter-culture district of Atlanta. In a very real way, it was created as art driven by anger against the religious rights repression.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the game grew beyond that, so assumptions and satire that was ok for it then isn't anymore. When it was written, the problem in the area was prejudice from ultra-conservative Christians against the more liberal Christians.<br /> <br /> But now the game reaches places and peoples with other problems in regard to religions, and they have other needs in relation to satire, other readings on the content, and so on. It's not just about making a less offensive narrative, but making a game that embraces more narratives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467822#post1467822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if he's an asshole, it's an endorsement of a kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem. Or, to be precise, the problem is that for some satirizing the ultra-conservative notion of God isn't enough compared to the problem of endorsing its existence in the first place. At least in some instances.<br /> <br /> I think this may be a good moment to make it clear: the satire on Christians that hold loads of prejudice and then say their God is good isn't lost on me, neither in VtM or DtF, and it is really fun. The problem is exclusively with the setting focusing it to the point that exploring other narratives is hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467822#post1467822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting case that the Gnostics are probably the LEAST incoherent religious interpretation of God because no decent deity would inflict such evil on their creations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setite belief as represented in the Path of Sutekh is one of the few <b>good</b> religions in the setting, explicitly demanding its followers to work for the well being of others.<br /> <br /> ==================================<br /> <br /> In the end, just to be clear, I don't think any of the issues that led to KotE being erased shouldn't be addressed. What I disagree is that erasing them is the best answer. The same way that I understand and actually live with many of the problems of Metis in Werewolf, yet don't think removing them from the game is the answer to the problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467843#post1467843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this was just after D&amp;D flipped its lid trying to cater to the BADD crowd as well as stripping &quot;demons&quot; and &quot;devils&quot; from the game as well as insisting it was family friendly as well as good for children.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side note, I think that was a good thing for D&amp;D in the end, as the Comics Code was a good thing for Comics. Being forced to develop their Tanar'ri and Baatezu as distinct as possible from classic demons and devils lead to a number of creative developments that wouldn't happen otherwise.<br /> <br /> When they went back to using Demons and Devils freely, combining those concepts had awesome results. It isn't that the decision was good, but it did create context for improvements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T06:43:17-08:00","id":1467877,"title":"","content":"V5 is very much about the simplification of the gameline. You can see it in everything from the way the Sabbat were treated to the way Disciplines were written. Quite frankly the Wan Kuei are far too complicated for V5, even just the basic concept of an alternative type of vampire. Further the Wan Kuei expressly reject some of the most basic components of V5's design philosophy such as the absolute focus on Humanity. Even the &quot;nicer&quot; Dharmas like the Dragons or Cranes are far too inhuman to fit into V5's wheelhouse let alone ones like the Devil Tigers or the Bone Flowers.<br /> <br /> Ultimately V5 has a very specific type of game it wants to tell and after what happened with the Sabbat, I just don't see the the Kindred of the East having a role in V5. In the end, V5 is simply not a game that has room for the sorts of stories that KotE wants to tell or the concepts that it wants players to explore. Even trying to convert the concepts like Dharma over to V5 is going to end up with those concepts being so watered down and diluted as to become completely flavorless. Better to just replace them with something entirely new.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* And just to note this isn't &quot;edition warring&quot; just acknowledging that the game V5 wants players to play is not the sort of game KotE wanted players to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-15-2021, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T07:52:17-08:00","id":1467880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467877#post1467877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 is very much about the simplification of the gameline. You can see it in everything from the way the Sabbat were treated to the way Disciplines were written. Quite frankly the Wan Kuei are far too complicated for V5, even just the basic concept of an alternative type of vampire. Further the Wan Kuei expressly reject some of the most basic components of V5's design philosophy such as the absolute focus on Humanity. Even the &quot;nicer&quot; Dharmas like the Dragons or Cranes are far too inhuman to fit into V5's wheelhouse let alone ones like the Devil Tigers or the Bone Flowers.<br /> <br /> Ultimately V5 has a very specific type of game it wants to tell and after what happened with the Sabbat, I just don't see the the Kindred of the East having a role in V5. In the end, V5 is simply not a game that has room for the sorts of stories that KotE wants to tell or the concepts that it wants players to explore. Even trying to convert the concepts like Dharma over to V5 is going to end up with those concepts being so watered down and diluted as to become completely flavorless. Better to just replace them with something entirely new.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* And just to note this isn't &quot;edition warring&quot; just acknowledging that the game V5 wants players to play is not the sort of game KotE wanted players to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edition warring for those who want to know how I interpret it is mainly an attempt to put down either V20 or V5 as a whole or its fans. You're free to dislike it but you have to define what the elements you dislike are.<br /> <br /> It's a narrow line to walk, I know, but it starts from the understanding that OPP produces games for V20, Chronicles of Darkness, and V5.<br /> <br /> You don't want to badmouth any of their lines on their forums.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T15:49:04-08:00","id":1467933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467877#post1467877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 is very much about the simplification of the gameline. You can see it in everything from the way the Sabbat were treated to the way Disciplines were written. Quite frankly the Wan Kuei are far too complicated for V5, even just the basic concept of an alternative type of vampire. Further the Wan Kuei expressly reject some of the most basic components of V5's design philosophy such as the absolute focus on Humanity. Even the &quot;nicer&quot; Dharmas like the Dragons or Cranes are far too inhuman to fit into V5's wheelhouse let alone ones like the Devil Tigers or the Bone Flowers.<br /> <br /> Ultimately V5 has a very specific type of game it wants to tell and after what happened with the Sabbat, I just don't see the the Kindred of the East having a role in V5. In the end, V5 is simply not a game that has room for the sorts of stories that KotE wants to tell or the concepts that it wants players to explore. Even trying to convert the concepts like Dharma over to V5 is going to end up with those concepts being so watered down and diluted as to become completely flavorless. Better to just replace them with something entirely new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I don't think it's to the degree your expressing, at least beyond the Rulebook. CotBG had several Cults with their own Convictions that weren't exactly humane. Same with most of the Cults themselves for that matter. And some of those Convictions were reminiscent of tenants of some Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> In fact while the upcoming V5 Sabbat does apparently attempt to regress the Sect back to NPC status, it is also bringing back the Paths of Enlightenment. The Dharmas aren't that far from the PoE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467843#post1467843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its kind of fascinating that V:TM never generated that kind of controversy as Dungeons and Dragons did--perhaps because it wore its defiance of social norms openly.<br /> <br /> (I mean it did generate quite a bit but not nearly as much)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of that is that when VtM first came out, the Satanic Panic of the 80s that fueled a lot of that controversy was dying off.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:12:37-08:00","id":1467956,"title":"","content":"Throwing my hat in on how to handle Eastern Vampires.<br /> <br /> Hungry Dead are, contrary to popular belief among Western Cainites, a unique clan of Kindred that have most of their Strongholds in East Asia. Their exact clan of origin is difficult to determine, both because of forgotten pre-history as well as the alterations of bloodlines produced by their unique process of Dharmic initiation. Most theories either hold them as being connected to the Tzimisce or the Cappadocians (due to their mutable natures and their associations with mortality) while other theories suggest that they developed as a unique Caitiff line. The Hungry dead generally reject the Caine myth and so do not put a lot of stock in pondering any prehistorical connection with Western Vampires. Instead they hold to their stories of the Yama Kings, powerfully ancient divine beings that punished the first of the Hungry Dead, dragging arrogant mortals into hell for their crimes. However these progenitors were not willing to accept the torment and fled from their imprisonment back to the world of the living, but not before the Yama Kings marked them with their curse, forcing them to live in shadows and subsist upon the lives of others to keep them from the call back to hell. Hungry Dead soon after learned that the curse could be passed on to others, tainting them with their impurities. Some spread their curse out of spite for the living, some out of a twisted sense of justice towards fellow sinners and criminals, some out of a pursuit of self-indulgent hunger for power, some simply to alleviate the loneliness of their cursed unlives. Whatever the reason, they spread throughout most of Asia and remain the most prolific clan there. One of the quirks of the blood of the hungry dead is that it does not appear to pass its potency as easily to childer. Newly embraced childer are quite uniformly low in potency, a side effect of which being that most arise from their embrace in a state of frenzy, a state that most Hungry dead claim is the result of one's soul temporarily passing into the torments of the Yama Kings in Hell before being brought back to the land of the living. As a result of the lack of pedigree that is offered by one's sire, as well as a mythology that holds the first among their kind as the first of a line of sinners rather than any great personhood, and the concept of Generation, as it is traditionally held among Western Kindred, is largely disregarded among the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> However what truly marks the hungry dead as distinct from Cainites are the Dharmas. Part blood sorcery, part spiritual philosophy, part social unit, the dharmas are a process of internal alchemy whereby the Hungry Dead begins a process of spiritual and supernatural enlightenment. Many Western Kindred have remarked upon the idea that the Dharmas are a form of Golconda path, and indeed, some kindred historians have pondered upon stories of an individual named by the Hungry Dead as Zao-Lat as one of those who helped standardize the five Dharmas within the Supernatural society of East Asia.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, functionally the Dharma path is a a long process by which a kindred is able to change themselves by holding to a disciplined mindset and regimen that is said to bring spiritual insights that in turn change their bodies. This not only seems to compensate for the difficulty of many Hungry dead face beginning at uniformly low blood potencies, it also seems to bypass many of the limits that generation might often present. Theoretically, any kindred following a Dharma could improve themselves without the limits of birthright, the upper limits being unknown but often spoken of in legends. However following Dharmas are a difficult path, and it is often easy for even the most dedicated adherent to even momentarily stray and ruin centuries of progress.<br /> <br /> While Hungry Dead are the most common variety of vampire in East Asia, they are not the only one, other clans have come to settle in Asia throughout history. Many among them have fully embraced the Dharmas, both out of an appeal to such methods as well as cultural pressure. Within most supernatural societies in East Asia, adherence to Dharmas is considered an essential moderating factor upon the often wild and disruptive actions of Kindred. Not only do the philosophies provide a motivation for a kindred to hold themselves to a higher purpose, but the teachers of Dharmas in a community are usually responsible for the actions of their students, and thus help keep them in check. By contrast, kindred who do not follow Dharma are usually considered dangerously unbound, regardless of their clan of origin, and such individuals are usually encouraged to move on their way.<br /> <br /> While Western Kindred have been blissfully ignorant of most of the details regarding their Eastern counterparts and vice versa, modern globalization has torn down those barriers and forced the two societies to confront one another. While many traiditionalists would prefer to continue ignoring one another as they stick to their own traditional hemispheres of power, others have been making moves, either diplomatically or with hostility. Cainites rode the ships of colonizers and established bases of power in many places such as Japan, Hong Kong and the Philippines, while Hungry Dead attempted to establish their own toeholds in California and further afield. Not every interaction has been a bloody one however. While it is not common, Western philosophically minded Kindred have been initiated into the the Dharmas before, while on the other side, ambitious hungry dead have found the politics of their Western counterparts more reactive and to their liking than the often glacial pace of a society rooted in the passive adherence to philosophies dictated by ancient beings more interested in their personal enlightenment than on the unlives of their followers.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's my basic headcanon. Hungry Dead are a clan of Kindred, but they reject the Caine myth even if a lot of Cainites might think that all of these Yama Kings sound like some kind of Antediluvian and/or their Methuselah childer. And more importantly they still tie themselves to Dharmas which would mechanically tie their generation and blood potency to their morality bar (which would have its own differences from humanity based on their Dharma), as well as granting them some more unique abilities (Discipline powers, as well as some of the bits like the ability to feed on breath or life force instead of blood as one advances). As mentioned, other clans could join a Dharma, but I'd imagine that would effectively alter them to some extent, like changing in-clan disciplines or even their curse to some extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T20:40:48-08:00","id":1467969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467933#post1467933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact while the upcoming V5 Sabbat does apparently attempt to regress the Sect back to NPC status, it is also bringing back the Paths of Enlightenment. The Dharmas aren't that far from the PoE.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the Sabbat book has no rules for Paths of Enlightenment because PoE are not something they want players in V5 to be on. Many of the Dharmas are require an even more dramatic shift shift away from Humanity than Paths of Enlightenment, and if White Wolf does not want Paths of Enlightenment in the player wheelhouse I have little reason to believe that Dharmas would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T23:51:54-08:00","id":1467976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467705#post1467705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the unfortunate implications that by making them also Cainites that makes the Abrahamic Faiths at least partly correct while making all other Faiths incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand where this is coming from, I have always found it head scratching that so many fans insist the WoD vampire origin myth means that Christianity is objectively real in the setting. Regardless of the origin myth we are told, there is absolutely nothing that establishes the Abrahamic religions are real or correct.<br /> <br /> When I first read the second edition VtM corebook many decades ago, I was already familiar with the idea that vampirism has its origins in the antedeluvian world as a curse with a founder among vampires. Why? That was basically the same story Marvel Comics used to explain vampires in their setting except that the antedeluvian world was Atlantis, the founder was Varnae, and the curse was a result of them being sorcerers using the Darkhold. Much later, its essentially the same story Mike Mignola used with the Black Goddess and Hyperborea in the Hellboy comics.<br /> <br /> The mentions of Caine, God, Nod, and everything else are just a patina that can be easily scrapped away. You can replace them with Chthon, Nyarlathotep, Tiamat, Atlantis, Hyperborea, Mu, and lots of other things.<br /> <br /> Do I think the vampires at the time of Alexander of the Great or Julius Caesar believe the eldest was Caine cursed by the Jewish Jehovah? Absolutely not. They most likely associated the antedeluvian world with the Flood of Deucalion and had some other explanation as to why vampirism existed (in my chronicles I tied it into the Orphic tradition of the Titans dismembering and eating Dionysus, his ichor mingling with others like how vitae mingles with human blood). Likewise the vampires of Ancient Sumeria wouldn't use a Jewish tradition that was not going to be used for thousands of years in the future! They'd be talking about the flood of Gilgamesh and might be referencing the antedeluvians as the Anunnaki.<br /> <br /> As so much that the origin of vampires is true as portrayed in the books, we only need to take seriously the core story. That there was a world before this one. The origins of vampires occurred there. That world was destroyed. And there were 13 survivors of that world that were the progenitors of all vampires today.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just details interpreted by vampires using their own cultural knowledge from their mortal days to understand what they've been told. The reason we have the Biblical centered myth of the corebook is because much of the world was ruled by either Christians or Muslims four two thousand years. I'm sure that any vampires originating in China likely use their own Flood traditions to explain the previous world, its destruction, and the vampire founders who survived. Same with other cultures. There just needs to be enough points in common so that the essential story is preserved, not the specific details.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T00:43:38-08:00","id":1467977,"title":"","content":"The game has spent a lot of wordcount on tying vampirism to Biblical mythology. There was even material like the Time of Judgment which ended up making those myths such as Caine, Abel, Lilith, etc as objective facts. In contrast the game has spent much less wordcount in offering alternatives to that myth, and so it can be hard for players to step away from it. Which, I think is entirely fair - the authors want players to focus heavily on the Biblical mythology, that's why they spend so much time and effort writing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-16-2021, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T01:11:05-08:00","id":1467978,"title":"","content":"For me, the obvious problems of the KJ can be boiled down to one word: Scope. <br /> <br /> They're too big and too disruptive. ALL asian vampires east of india are KJ, plus a few western cainites that have surrendered to them in order to live in their territory. They KILL all the foreigners and have invaded california because... Americans were convinced the Japanese economy would never stop growing when White wolf were making games. If the Cathayans were a mysterious/reclusive bunch that didn't overstep their bounds and make it their unlife's goal to unreasonably shit on cainites, all this ugly would've been avoided. I think the KJ are mechanically and, refering to their dharmas and wronged ghost shtick, thematically compelling. <br /> <br /> If they must be made into Cainites, i'd like the following<br /> <br /> Dharma is path. The groups that use Dharmas don't use humanity. <br /> The Cathayans have lots of small sects that only promote a few Dharmas each. There's lots of room for ST's to set up their own. <br /> The Camarilla are a big contender in Asia, and most members of the Asian Camarilla are asian, not european, because the Camarilla is a global sect that's been in Asia for 400 years or so. The Camarilla/Sect conflict is more about old VS New, with the Camarilla being mostly younger vampires with a better grasp on modernity. The Camarilla takes a lot of cues from Anarchs in a western game: often playing scrappy modern underdogs. This is not to say that the Dharma sects don't have neonates or the occasional elders that embrace modernity, but they certainly have more individuals that reject it. <br /> The Sabbat exists, but mostly plays second fiddle to local Dharma sects. <br /> Anarchs are kind of unthinkable. The Camarilla represents the young, and sure it could use some change, but you've got dinosaurs on the horizon. <br /> <br /> <br /> A few clan-bloodline variations wouldn't be so bad, but I think perhaps a hopping vampire would be too much strain on the Masquerade, so I'd keep it as a myth, or perhaps a side-effect of some thaumaturgy ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T02:51:43-08:00","id":1467979,"title":"","content":"Oddly I've never really had a problem with them, they don't really mesh very well with Asian mysticism but then again vtm don't really mesh with anything beyond 20th century pop culture vampire either. Ultimatly I've always had a good time when I played it and the dharma mysticism is quite a solid role-playing opertunity.<br /> On subject the dharmas as clan does have some precedence in v5b since the Sabbat book treats paths as a rough equivalent of clan/character class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-16-2021, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T09:28:30-08:00","id":1468012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467978#post1467978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They KILL all the foreigners and have invaded california because... Americans were convinced the Japanese economy would never stop growing when White wolf were making games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a weird take, since the bubble was already visibly burst when Second Edition was being published, and a good six years before KotE.<br /> <br /> I was busy being 10 in '92, but far as I can see, here in America the notion of 'oh god Japan is going to own the world' really only seems to pop up in stuff (fictional or otherwise) dating from the '80s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T10:07:09-08:00","id":1468019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1467978#post1467978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the obvious problems of the KJ can be boiled down to one word: Scope.<br /> <br /> They're too big and too disruptive. ALL asian vampires east of india are KJ, plus a few western cainites that have surrendered to them in order to live in their territory. They KILL all the foreigners and have invaded california because... Americans were convinced the Japanese economy would never stop growing when White wolf were making games. If the Cathayans were a mysterious/reclusive bunch that didn't overstep their bounds and make it their unlife's goal to unreasonably shit on cainites, all this ugly would've been avoided. I think the KJ are mechanically and, refering to their dharmas and wronged ghost shtick, thematically compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take was it wasn't so much RL metaphor and influence but the attempt to shill the Kuei Jin to fans [into buying the books].<br /> <br /> &quot;You see, we have this new splat of Asian Vampires and they are WAY MORE BADASS than the Cainites. In fact they look down at Cainites because they're losers! They can step sideways, they have caerns, and they fight demons! Oh and they kill all Cainites in their territory but those who submitted because they're that awesome. How awesome are they? They invaded the California Free States and wiped out the Anarchs! Oh yeah, now it's all Kuei Jin territory!&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, they're Serpentor in GI Joe. Except GI Joe fans hated Serpentor for being mean to Cobra Commander and stomping all over him so they were glad when Cobra Commander came back and kicked his ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468012#post1468012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a weird take, since the bubble was already visibly burst when Second Edition was being published, and a good six years before KotE.<br /> <br /> I was busy being 10 in '92, but far as I can see, here in America the notion of 'oh god Japan is going to own the world' really only seems to pop up in stuff (fictional or otherwise) dating from the '80s.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, certain subsets were already viewing the Japanese Tiger economy as being replaced by the Chinese.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:01:32-08:00","id":1468033,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to me that you have all this pop theme of Japan taking over California, but I see little reference to the sizable Japanese community in Hawaii. Do they have some impact in this imagery?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know how much the <i>theme</i>of a Japanese presence there depend on the <i>fear</i> of Japanese growth at the time. What I do know is that some Japanese games, upon translation, have cities like T\u014dky\u014d replaced by San Francisco, which creates a funny confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:54:09-08:00","id":1468042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468033#post1468033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to me that you have all this pop theme of Japan taking over California, but I see little reference to the sizable Japanese community in Hawaii. Do they have some impact in this imagery?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know how much the <i>theme</i>of a Japanese presence there depend on the <i>fear</i> of Japanese growth at the time. What I do know is that some Japanese games, upon translation, have cities like T\u014dky\u014d replaced by San Francisco, which creates a funny confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking over Hawaii wouldn't be a deliberate slap to the Anarchs and a sign they were no longer part of the game's vision.<br /> <br /> But that may be a bitter interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-16-2021, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T14:18:08-08:00","id":1468050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468042#post1468042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking over Hawaii wouldn't be a deliberate slap to the Anarchs and a sign they were no longer part of the game's vision.<br /> <br /> But that may be a bitter interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's an interesting comparison to be made with the V5 Sabbat here then. The Anarchs in revised certainly got shellacked as far as the fall of the free states, but they still ended up getting their own distinct hardcover afterwards with rules for playing them and all sorts of other things in it, intended for pc use no less. They even got to be a presence in the New York by Night citybook, with their own significant territory and political figures that had decent heft and influence.<br /> <br /> Which is interesting when, pre V5 existing, people liked to call Revised the most judgy of the VtM editions (Revised has a special place in my heart for being the edition I did *most* of my VtM gaming with until V20, but even I admit it *loved* to judge you for not playing how it wanted you to), but all the same it still offered play support for things you could argue were not in the game's vision anymore (I mean, not the True Black Hand, one grants, but the Anarchs managed to still be in the mix).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-16-2021, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:04:11-08:00","id":1468053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468042#post1468042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking over Hawaii wouldn't be a deliberate slap to the Anarchs and a sign they were no longer part of the game's vision.<br /> <br /> But that may be a bitter interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, not just that, but I'm thinking if the Japanese presence in Hawaii have any impact in this pop picture of the Japanese overtaking the West Coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:12:20-08:00","id":1468055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468053#post1468053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, not just that, but I'm thinking if the Japanese presence in Hawaii have any impact in this pop picture of the Japanese overtaking the West Coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Mike Pondsmith and some conversations he had that I paid attention to back in the early Nineties, he believed it was primarily motivated by a sense of unearned American outrage over the purchase of several American locations like the Rockerfeller Center. Mind you, Mike also stated that cyberpunk and capitalism had a weird envy/resentment duality. At its best, he suggested it was a critique of American exceptionalism and the idea that it wouldn't eventually lose its dominion over capitalism the same way Great Britain and the Empire did.<br /> <br /> At its worst, they seemed to think Asian ascendency was somehow a element of the dystopia versus a sign no one really wins forever in capitalism.<br /> <br /> In White Wolf's case, I believe the takeover of the West Coast wa because the Anarch Free States were considered disposable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T18:12:21-08:00","id":1468083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468053#post1468053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, not just that, but I'm thinking if the Japanese presence in Hawaii have any impact in this pop picture of the Japanese overtaking the West Coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was just the logical extension. <br /> <br /> WW released the KotE books, but there were complaints that those books were mostly useless unless people were setting games specifically in Asia. If your games were mainly set in the US (which most games at the time were) why would you bother purchasing the KotE gameline? So WW introduced a story element to bring the eastern kindred to the US where they would be more available for gaming, and also as a way to encourage people to buy the books. Of course, this being the World of Darkness where everyone is at one another's throats in an eternal conflict, that ended up being an effective invasion. And the East Coast was chosen as opposed to say, the Deep South because of demographics - that is, there were much larger existing Asian-American communities on the East Coast than there in other parts of the US.<br /> <br /> Basically WW wanted more people to buy the KotE books they were publishing, so they had an event take place in one of the more popular parts of the setting to get people to buy the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T06:10:47-08:00","id":1468121,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Seriously, please stop national stereotyping.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T07:22:01-08:00","id":1468129,"title":"","content":"Was that directed towards me? Cathayans are composed almost entirely from people in Asia or of Asiatic descent. That's how KotE works. And according to US census data almost half of people who say they are of Asiatic descent live in California and up the East Coast. The rest are roughly spread out in the US with the smallest proportion of that demographic living in in places like Arkansas, Georgia, etc. You can see that demographic data <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_Asian_Americans\" target=\"_blank\">here for youself if you would like.</a><br /> <br /> I honestly don't feel stating simple facts like those is engaging in stereotyping. If you feel otherwise I will stop discussing this subject. My apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-17-2021, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T08:34:37-08:00","id":1468137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467679-v5-kindred-of-the-east-clan-as-dharmas?p=1468129#post1468129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that directed towards me?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he deleted the offending post IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"u