, and Western kindred being another where one or more ancient examples mutated in such a way as to make their undead state transmissible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T09:48:07-08:00","id":1470284,"title":"","content":"Hear me out, the way to fix the KotE is actually right infront of you in the KotE book it self, and Wraith The Oblivion 20th.<br /> <br /> The KotE are not Vampires, they are originally wraiths that are Risen. So why the difference from Stygian Risen? Easy, in Stygia, the process/ritual is not only rare in the Western branch of the underworld but highly illegal. <br /> <br /> In the Dark Kingdom of Jade, they have a different culture, wich causes a different relationship with thier dark half and Oblivion. This causes difference in how thier Shadow/po, and Psyche/hun is viewed. It is also why Pathos/yin and Angst/Yang doesn't cause as much issue with the wraiths of the Jade Kingdom, as much as the they do for Stygia. Is either side wrong, no. It's each side has a different relationship with thier environment. They also use very different rituals to initiate the process to become a Risen, add to the fact that the ritual is also not only not as illegal, think misdemeanor, but also more openly shared. The Various Dharmas, plus the regional tricks developed in the skinlands led to different &quot;types&quot; of the eastern vampires appearing such as the Hopping Vampires of China, the female fillipino, or the floating heads of Malaysia. All using different applications of thier disciplines. <br /> Remember that Western Risen can learn some vampire disciplines, and develop new ones as well. <br /> <br /> Again, the KotE are not Vampires, they are Wraiths that use a different kind of ritual to reanimate thier body that keeps the shadow/po in thier body. This ritual how ever initially causes thier body to be considered a creature of darkness which causes thier body to rot initially, some thing about the Sun and the Scarlet Queen and Ebon Dragon not liking each other...<br /> <br /> Any way, so do the KotE hate the Cainites, let's just say the Cainites stink of tge old European colonialism and barbarian invaders, what with thier ability to spread like herpes,and they occupy the similar ecological niche as them, and there were those incidents with the Antidiluvians of Solubri and Ravenos<br /> That put the bad taste in thier mouth. <br /> Remember Western Wraiths become Risen to finish unresolved buisiness, Eastern Wraiths do so to escape the Hells of the Yama Kings, and reach enlightenment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T07:18:04-08:00","id":1502103,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I'm answering doing a real necroposting work but I'm picking up KotE in view of a future V5 campaign.<br /> I am contextualizing the Kuei-jin as the descendants of the Cainites they followed lost tribes of Israel to the east in particular those of Dan and Ephraim mentioned by the Apocalypse as the only ones who at the end of time will not have salvation who settled in the east 600 years before Christ.<br /> Far from their clans and from the wars between sects, they have rebuilt a new society based on the clash between P'o and Hun between Ying and Yang.<br /> In this context I recreated the Dharmas simply as a Cult (following the rules of CotBG) and treating all vampires like Caitiff\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25636-benkalas","user":"Benkalas","date":". 02-04-2023, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25636-benkalas","name":"Benkalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25636_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}